{
  "summary": "No CRITICAL or HIGH vulnerabilities were identified. URL scheme validation and redirect handling correctly restrict destinations to HTTP(S), and short codes use cryptographically strong randomness. Medium-risk hardening issues remain around unbounded input, trusted Host header construction, and unrestricted endpoint access.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "file": "src/main/java/com/example/shortener/LinkCreateRequest.java",
      "issue": "The submitted URL has no maximum-length validation. Although the JPA column is limited to 2048 characters, arbitrarily large JSON strings can be parsed and processed before persistence. Oversized values may also cause repeated database failures because LinkService catches DataIntegrityViolationException and retries code generation.",
      "recommendation": "Add an explicit maximum length constraint, such as @Size(max = 2048), and enforce an HTTP request-body size limit at the server or reverse proxy. Map oversized input to HTTP 400 without attempting persistence retries."
    },
    {
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "file": "src/main/java/com/example/shortener/LinkController.java",
      "issue": "buildShortUrl constructs public URLs directly from request.getScheme(), getServerName(), and getServerPort(). If the service is reachable with an untrusted Host header or is deployed behind a proxy without strict forwarded-header handling, an attacker can cause API responses and the Location header of link creation to contain an attacker-controlled origin. This can enable host-header poisoning, phishing links, or cache poisoning.",
      "recommendation": "Use a configured canonical public base URL, or strictly validate trusted proxy headers and the Host header against an allow-list. Do not derive externally advertised URLs from arbitrary request headers."
    },
    {
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "file": "src/main/java/com/example/shortener/RedirectController.java",
      "issue": "The redirect endpoint has no rate limiting or abuse control. Although seven-character random codes provide a large search space, unrestricted requests permit sustained code-guessing, link existence probing through 404 versus 302 responses, and click-count inflation for discovered links.",
      "recommendation": "Add rate limiting and monitoring for redirect and creation endpoints, preferably keyed by client/network identity with suitable proxy-aware controls. Consider additional abuse detection for high-volume invalid-code probing."
    },
    {
      "severity": "LOW",
      "file": "src/main/java/com/example/shortener/LinkController.java",
      "issue": "The code path variable is not constrained to the generated seven-character URL-safe format. Arbitrary path values are accepted and queried, increasing database work for probing requests and allowing malformed code inputs to reach the repository.",
      "recommendation": "Constrain the route or validate codes before repository access using exactly seven characters from [A-Za-z0-9_-], and reject other values with a consistent 404 or 400 response."
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "title": "Treat destination redirects as intentional rather than an open redirect",
      "rationale": "The service is explicitly required to redirect known codes to their stored destinations. UrlValidator restricts creation to absolute HTTP and HTTPS URLs and rejects javascript:, data:, file:, relative, and malformed values, so the redirect behavior itself is not an unintended open redirect.",
      "alternatives": [
        "Report the redirect endpoint as an open redirect, which would conflict with the stated URL-shortener functionality.",
        "Require a destination-domain allow-list, which is outside the supplied requirements."
